WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.853
Advanced view is the full node canvas.

2
00:00:02.853 --> 00:00:05.404
Maximize the Controls window to give it room.

3
00:00:05.404 --> 00:00:08.409
The palette on the left lists every node by category.

4
00:00:08.869 --> 00:00:11.261
Click a palette item to add a node.

5
00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:11.740
An LFO.

6
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:12.287
A Clock.

7
00:00:12.287 --> 00:00:13.791
And a Sample and Hold.

8
00:00:16.135 --> 00:00:19.803
Drag nodes by their headers to lay the patch out, left to right.

9
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.646
Drag from an output dot to an input dot.

10
00:00:22.646 --> 00:00:25.091
The LFO into the Sample and Hold's input.

11
00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.179
The Clock's pulse into its trigger.

12
00:00:27.629 --> 00:00:30.014
Click a node to edit it in the inspector.

13
00:00:30.014 --> 00:00:33.155
Speed the LFO up, so every sample lands somewhere new.

14
00:00:33.607 --> 00:00:35.452
Bindings send a node to the synth.

15
00:00:35.452 --> 00:00:38.111
Add a binding from the Sample and Hold to Z Push.

16
00:00:38.563 --> 00:00:41.055
Probe draws a live trace of any output.

17
00:00:41.055 --> 00:00:44.507
Stepped values: the classic sample and hold staircase.

18
00:00:44.966 --> 00:00:46.142
Restore the window.

19
00:00:46.142 --> 00:00:49.610
The depth now jumps to a new random level on every beat.

20
00:00:50.059 --> 00:00:54.147
Every node works this way: outputs to inputs, bindings to the synth.

21
00:00:54.147 --> 00:00:56.792
Next, two pictures at once with Dual Raster.
